me> <mountpoint> -o url=http{s}://<COS_endpoint> –o passwd_file=<credentials_file> -o cipher_suites=AESGCM -o kernel_cache -o max_background=1000 -o max_stat_cache_size=100000 -o multipart_size=52 -o parallel_count=30 -o multireq_max=30 -o dbglevel=warn\n\n\n\n\n\n1. cipher_suites=AESGCM is only relevant when using an HTTPS endpoint.",
    "statements": [
        "Enter the name of the already-provisioned Object Storage bucket.",
        "Enter the Object Storage endpoint for the bucket, such as https://s3.dal.us.cloud-object-storage.appdomain.cloud.",
        "Enter the IBM Cloud API key.",
        "Mount the bucket as a directory using s3fs.",
        "The s3fs mount command requires the bucket name, mount point, COS endpoint, and credentials file.",
        "The documented performance-oriented mount command is: s3fs <bucket_name> <mountpoint> -o url=http{s}://<COS_endpoint> -o passwd_file=<credentials_file> -o cipher_suites=AESGCM -o kernel_cache -o max_background=1000 -o max_stat_cache_size=100000 -o multipart_size=52 -o parallel_count=30 -o multireq_max=30 -o dbglevel=warn.",
        "After mounting, the command ls <mountpoint> lists the bucket objects as local files.",
        "The cipher_suites=AESGCM option applies only with an HTTPS endpoint.",
        "The answer cites page 1 as the source of the documented instructions."
    ]
}
